# Backend Standards (PHP + mysqli)

## Tenant & Role Guard

- `TenantGuard::requireTenant()` to fetch tenant_id from session/JWT.

- `TenantGuard::requireRole([...])` on every endpoint.

## Data Access

- All queries include tenant filtering.

- Validate overlaps for shifts per person (no overlapping time windows).

- Allow multi-client per day by splitting shifts; only the overlap is forbidden.

## Endpoints (minimum set)

- `/api/planner.php?path=events` GET: unified calendar feed (WO/Assignments/Shifts/Requests).

- `/api/planner.php?path=slot` POST: create/modify slots.

- `/api/project-schedule.php` POST: create multi-day slots by weekday selection.

- `/api/shifts.php`: list/create/update/split/merge/reassign/status/bulk.

## Responses

- JSON canonical: `{ data, meta }` or `{ error: { code, message } }`.

- Use prepared statements, handle errors centrally.
